alizing, not just what's presented with Loopholes and Icons and Goblin Debt and Galoshins, but what's left beneath the surface unspoken. I think I can work with this, yes.<br /> <br /> Furrowing my eyebrows a bit at the Shadowsoul and Telluric Blessings. Maybe I just don't Get It yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am curious as to how the Shadow Soul and Telluric blessings have been rebooted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T22:45:05-07:00","id":1490764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490756#post1490756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> I am curious as to how the Shadow Soul and Telluric blessings have been rebooted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shadowsouls: +Wyrd on Subterfuge (instead of Intimidate), 8 again on Subterfuge (instead of 9 again), Mirror Regalia as affinity instead of Contracts of Darkness. Once per scene they can inflict Blindness for the rest of the scene on the target of an exceptional attack (this one is new).<br /> <br /> Telluric: 3 successes for exceptional on chases where they can see the stars. The ability to throw a Damage 1 fireball for 1 Glamour.<br /> <br /> There's a new Kith with timing based abilities called Climacteric.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19862-jadeite","name":"jadeite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-19T23:17:21-07:00","id":1490765,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>jadeite</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490764#post1490764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Shadowsouls: +Wyrd on Subterfuge (instead of Intimidate), 8 again on Subterfuge (instead of 9 again), Mirror Regalia as affinity instead of Contracts of Darkness. Once per scene they can inflict Blindness for the rest of the scene on the target of an exceptional attack (this one is new).<br /> <br /> Telluric: 3 successes for exceptional on chases where they can see the stars. The ability to throw a Damage 1 fireball for 1 Glamour.<br /> <br /> There's a new Kith with timing based abilities called Climacteric.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> What is the Climacteric blessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T01:39:56-07:00","id":1490772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490765#post1490765\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> What is the Climacteric blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>They get an exceptional success on 3 on Investigation rolls to detect patterns and can make someone else act first on the initiative order for one glamour.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19862-jadeite","name":"jadeite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T11:09:05-07:00","id":1490806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490658#post1490658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's quite a packed book. Still digesting, finding myself jumping back and forth between sections, reading out of order, seeing what grabs me, what's going to take some time to settle in.<br /> <br /> Dramaturgy as a general principle is very intriguing. The possibilities it suggests are tantalizing, not just what's presented with Loopholes and Icons and Goblin Debt and Galoshins, but what's left beneath the surface unspoken. I think I can work with this, yes.<br /> <br /> Furrowing my eyebrows a bit at the Shadowsoul and Telluric Blessings. Maybe I just don't Get It yet.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I am very curious as to what the books explores, besides kiths. As the title includes <i><b>Kin</b></i>, does it introduce fae blooded or explore the fae touched in greater detail?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T18:07:40-07:00","id":1490832,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490806#post1490806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am very curious as to what the books explores, besides kiths. As the title includes <i><b>Kin</b></i>, does it introduce fae blooded or explore the fae touched in greater detail?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the Changeling 2e Player's Guide, much as Flowers of Hell was Demon: the Descent's Player's Guide.<br /> <br /> There's a bunch of new Contracts, a bunch of new types of pledge (including a specifically-magically-oriented modification of bargains that lets you allow someone to see through the Mask, a means of anteing one of your possessions to make pursuing an Aspiration more rewarding, establishing mystically-enforced rules for an event, and straight-up cursing people), discussions of some new notable subsections of the Hedge (the BriarNet gets a proper address here, and the Wishing Roads are introduced as a set of trods that connect both space and abandoned hopes/dreams/wishes), a deeper look at Regalia (including a system for manifesting one of your Regalia onto a powerful token or stranger things), and a discussion of the aforementioned dramaturgy system (which interacts with Loopholes, temporary mystical identity theft, and basically the entire framework in which hobgoblins do their work).<br /> <br /> There's also a fairly in-depth discussion of changeling psychology (including variant Touchstone mechanics and a couple of alternatives to Comatose for characters who hit Clarity 0), a lengthy discussion of motleys, and a number of new safety tools.<br /> <br /> On the &quot;Kith&quot; end of things, there's also mechanics for being kithless (three different ways, the more unusual pair of which come with their own interesting drawbacks, while the standard means offers what I would consider a reasonable tradeoff for kithlessness in the form of a kind of broad pseudo-kith-blessing) and acquiring a kith (also three different ways, the least involved of which is &quot;getting a secondhand kith from a hobgoblin who has one available, which might come with leftover Goblin Debt whose creditor you'll need to figure out,&quot; while the other two involve incorporating another changeling's Icon or undertaking an ordeal with a Condition not unlike the Founder's Mark one takes upon trying to forge a court).<br /> <br /> It's a hundred and forty-odd pages of New Material, a good chunk of which is new kiths because the Kickstarter had multiple stretch goals dedicated to adding more kiths to the book. It's sufficiently full of Content that all I'm really still waiting for to be confident I can finish getting setup ready for transitioning my Changeling playtest game to 2e proper (besides player schedule alignment) is to see what material The Hedge will contain for consideration.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T19:21:22-07:00","id":1490838,"title":"","content":"I haven't had time to read through the whole thing comprehensively yet, but I have to say that the BriarNet is a really interesting concept. I'm definitely designing some dark web-esque goblin markets.<br /> <br /> It's also nice to see the returning first edition kiths; it's like meeting old friends again. Since second edition kiths are not tied to seemings, it's going to be a real treat brainstorming how those kiths look on changelings with different seemings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T20:09:22-07:00","id":1490841,"title":"","content":"I am curious as to whether any of the kiths from Changeling 1.5 have made it into the book. Is the Dear Heart kith in <b><i>Kith and Kin</i></b>? If so, how has its blessing been rebooted?<br /> <br /> Also what about the Gravewright and Oracle kiths? Have their blessings been rebooted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T21:03:10-07:00","id":1490843,"title":"","content":"Gravewrights are back, and they still have the Charnel Sight blessing. Oracles and Dearhearts haven't returned, as far as I can tell.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26495-shinsoryuu","name":"Shinsoryuu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26495_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T21:22:05-07:00","id":1490844,"title":"","content":"The Oracle became the Sideromancer.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>chloe \u2022 onyx path freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24091-fiercefully","name":"fiercefully","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T21:39:49-07:00","id":1490845,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490841#post1490841\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also what about the Gravewright and Oracle kiths? Have their blessings been rebooted?</div> </div> </div> </div>Gravewights are in the unsorted category of kiths with their Charnel Sight returning with a Glamour cost. Oracles have not returned under that name, but there's a divining kith called the Sideromancer whose trickery is also called Panomancy, albeit its mechanics now allow you to use it more frequently but more narrowly and with a Glamour cost.<br /> <br /> Dearhearts are not in the book, though their described niche fits more than one kith on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T21:55:57-07:00","id":1490846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490845#post1490845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gravewights are in the unsorted category of kiths with their Charnel Sight returning with a Glamour cost. Oracles have not returned under that name, but there's a divining kith called the Sideromancer whose trickery is also called Panomancy, albeit its mechanics now allow you to use it more frequently but more narrowly and with a Glamour cost.<br /> <br /> Dearhearts are not in the book, though their described niche fits more than one kith on the list.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Has Charnel Sight been updated in anyway? Does the Gravewight treat three successes as an exceptional success when dealing with ghosts?<br /> <br /> How does the Sideromancer's Panomancery work and how is it different compared to the previous Oracle's Panomancery?<br /> <br /> Finally, what are the kiths whose niche fits the Dearhearts? Has the Succubi/Inccubi kith been reintroduced?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-20T23:36:53-07:00","id":1490847,"title":"","content":"The contract seem kinda... not super well balanced or straight up doesn't follow normal rules for how the book describes Resisted and Contested powers. For example Beggar Knight it's resisted but it's effect is binary. Either you get hit with the power or not which means it should be Contested. The only bonus for additional success is to extend the duration.<br /> The Golden Vow contract needs some cleaning up in it's language as it seems to mix and match Services and Equipment purchases.<br /> Coin Mark just straight out doesn't offer any resistance. The list goes on.<br /> <br /> Overall the book seems neat with lots of good ideas but not super impressed with some of the editing as others have mentioned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12824-bloodyquill","name":"Bloodyquill","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T01:21:45-07:00","id":1490852,"title":"","content":"I don't get Star Light, Star Bright. You get to know a person's recent wish but have to fulfill it (or be branded an oathbreaker), with no additional help from the Contract to do so. You can spend an additional Glamour to add a drawback, but it still seems pointless in comparison to Contracts of Spring (like Cupid's Arrow which is Common instead of Royal).<br /> Other Contracts seem quite strong, like Closing Death's Door, Witch's Brambles or Steal Influence.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19862-jadeite","name":"jadeite","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T05:58:57-07:00","id":1490869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bloodyquill</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490847#post1490847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The list goes on.</div> </div> </div> </div>The errata form is still open and has a category for Mechanics-related wrinkles. Submit the issue there so it's on the list.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T06:17:08-07:00","id":1490873,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490846#post1490846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Has Charnel Sight been updated in anyway?</div> </div> </div> </div>Costs Glamour to activate now.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the Gravewight treat three successes as an exceptional success when dealing with ghosts? </div> </div> </div>Set choice of Empathy or Intimidation to influence someone with their mien, physical presence, or knowledge of the mechanics of death.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How does the Sideromancer's Panomancery work and how is it different compared to the previous Oracle's Panomancery? </div> </div> </div>1e Panomancy was &quot;Once per chapter you can choose to benefit from the effects of the Common Sense Merit (doesn't count as using the Merit if you also have the Merit).&quot; 2e Panomancy lets you roll Wits + Occult + Wyrd to get your successes in yes/no questions answered about the same-scene consequences of your being party to the making of a promise or pledge or the incurrence or payment of a debt.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, what are the kiths whose niche fits the Dearhearts? Has the Succubi/Inccubi kith been reintroduced? </div> </div> </div>Polychromatics and Concubi come to mind most readily.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:25:44-07:00","id":1490896,"title":"","content":"The Wishing Roads, BriarNet, and time bullshit were all exactly as much fun to right as you seem to be having reading them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:36:55-07:00","id":1490899,"title":"","content":"Damn all this teasing. I just want the briarnet at this point","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24173-primordial-newcomer","name":"Primordial newcomer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1965"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T10:51:35-07:00","id":1490903,"title":"","content":"Still mulling over my copy. One thing I'm working on is a homebrew Regalia for my setting of Buena Vista called Card with themes of games, rules, strategy, wagers, and a bit of divination. Going to be putting my own version of Game Master's Table as one of its royal contracts. The BriarNet is also relevant to my interests, since BV's Hedge has a bit of sci-fi flavoring.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10118-bronzedog","name":"BronzeDog","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"239"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T15:50:45-07:00","id":1490943,"title":"","content":"Got a few more ordered thoughts on everything now. Let's see here. . .<br /> <br /> The Veneficus makes me realize that there are probably a number of First Edition entitlements that would work better as kiths in the 2e paradigm.<br /> <br /> Some of the tone of the BriarNet and Wishing Roads write-ups reads as maybe a little too whimsical to me for a horror game, but I'm going to chalk that up to differences in personal taste rather than a fatal flaw in the design. At least now we have a way of recreating Reboot or Digimon. (Come to think of it, the plot of Digimon World is basically a Changeling story, isn't it?) The lunar freehold and general outer space parts feel very unintroduced outside the sidebar about doing what's best for your own game. That said, I think there are some intentional parallels between the Outer Hedge and some bits of other parts of Chronicles cosmology. Next you'll tell me there's an ocean in the Hedge on whose shores an affable old man dwells in a hut.<br /> <br /> Sub-thought to that: Arcadia is certainly a realm where the facts of yourself can be taken out and reconfigured.<br /> <br /> Sub-sub-thought: . . .<i>Oh.</i><br /> <br /> You'd think after the Contagion Chronicle releasing when it did, Onyx Path writers would have thrown up their hands at the prospect of putting content warnings on disease-related material. I respect the intent though.<br /> <br /> The parameters for Hexes could be better defined. I think the system is a little too open-ended as is, or could use further contextualization. I guess this encompasses most of my criticisms of the book, that there are parts where rules need to be clarified or at least situated in context. What does it mean that the Wisewitch can &quot;form pledges with spirits and angels&quot;? What does the Oculus trickery actually do, mechanics-wise? Ah well, here we are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T16:59:48-07:00","id":1490953,"title":"","content":"The BriarNet was 100% written with ReBoot in mind, shortly followed by Digimon. I suspect most people will go for Tron over ReBoot, but I appreciate that some people see the seed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-21T18:05:55-07:00","id":1490958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490953#post1490953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BriarNet was 100% written with ReBoot in mind, shortly followed by Digimon. I suspect most people will go for Tron over ReBoot, but I appreciate that some people see the seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I LOVED Digimon as a kid. I hope that in the Hedge book we are introduced to Digi Hedgebeasts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T05:28:09-07:00","id":1490988,"title":"","content":"There's too much exciting stuff in this book to decide what to start with but I do want to take a moment to appreciate that someone took the time and page space to make <i>not</i> having a kith interesting and finding at least three different ways to do it that sound as interesting as any kith or more.<br /> <br /> Dramaturgy I was a little disappointed by at first, hoping for something with more specific mechanics that might come up more often, but I came around on it pretty quickly. It's a cool way to outline some of the deeper flavor under a lot of Wyrd magic and provides some great signposting for STs trying to figure out what the &quot;true cost&quot; of an exchange at the goblin market might be or players who want to try to ride the wave of hedge weirdness and fae logic to pull off something dangerous and clever.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T07:25:01-07:00","id":1490995,"title":"","content":"Is the Awestruck condition in any Changeling sources? It comes up a few time for Fairest versions of contracts, but for the life of me I cannot find out what it actually does and it seems to only be in the Werewolf core book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6927-gillestrilleuze","name":"GillesTrilleuze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T08:27:28-07:00","id":1490998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GillesTrilleuze</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490995#post1490995\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the Awestruck condition in any Changeling sources? It comes up a few time for Fairest versions of contracts, but for the life of me I cannot find out what it actually does and it seems to only be in the Werewolf core book.</div> </div> </div> </div>P. 333-334 of Changeling 2e","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T10:47:22-07:00","id":1491011,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I didn't realize that I had an old version of the core book downloaded where it hadn't been added yet. Updated on DRPG and it's there!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6927-gillestrilleuze","name":"GillesTrilleuze","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T15:52:32-07:00","id":1491050,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490953#post1490953\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The BriarNet was 100% written with ReBoot in mind, shortly followed by Digimon. I suspect most people will go for Tron over ReBoot, but I appreciate that some people see the seed.</div> </div> </div> </div>I loved ReBoot and definitely saw the seeds of it in the BriarNet. I have a number of ideas to put a Hexidecimal like character into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/898-kurasu","name":"kurasu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar898_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-22T16:36:36-07:00","id":1491055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1490832#post1490832\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a hundred and forty-odd pages of New Material, a good chunk of which is new kiths because the Kickstarter had multiple stretch goals dedicated to adding more kiths to the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>That explains it. I'll be honest; I'm sad about how fifty-one three to five paragraphs for each kith has somehow muddled what each kith is and does. As espritdecalimar says, there is eyebrow-furrowing at more than a few kith bonuses, and more than a few kith write-ups. It breaks my heart to say this as Changeling has been my go-to WoD system since day one.<br /> <br /> There is a lot to love in this book, and even the things I don't care for are still quite interesting and worth the read. (Freehold on the Moooooon!) But as the Making Kiths section says, take what you want and leave the rest. As long as it fits your table, that's the key takeaway.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T12:16:44-07:00","id":1491228,"title":"","content":"yeah, so ... while i am really digging this book, the power disparity amongst the various contracts and kith blessings can be pretty wild (eg: witches brambles or the witchtooth's kith blessing).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T13:33:49-07:00","id":1491236,"title":"","content":"(Deleted because responding to something on a much earlier page)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T17:38:46-07:00","id":1491260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491228#post1491228\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah, so ... while i am really digging this book, the power disparity amongst the various contracts and kith blessings can be pretty wild (eg: witches brambles or the witchtooth's kith blessing).</div> </div> </div> </div> What is the difference between Witche's Bramble and the Withtooths blessing? I am assuming Witches Brambles is a contract (Probably Autumn or Goblin), but what are it's affects? Are they similiar to the Witchtooth's blessing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T19:11:20-07:00","id":1491265,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491260#post1491260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the difference between Witche's Bramble and the Withtooths blessing? I am assuming Witches Brambles is a contract (Probably Autumn or Goblin), but what are it's affects? Are they similiar to the Witchtooth's blessing?</div> </div> </div> </div>Witch's Brambles is a Royal Thorn Contract that lets the user perform Hedgespinning in the mortal realm under certain stipulations. The Witchtooth Trickery allows the changeling to &quot;reshape the land within one mile to look however she wants it to.&quot; What this means pre-errata is a little vague, though does impose a -1 penalty to Survival rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-24T19:28:57-07:00","id":1491267,"title":"","content":"I am designing a chronicle where Edgar Allen Poe is a Darkling with the author kith and his wife, Anna Bell Lee, is a fairest with the Water Kith. Has the Author kith made it into the Kith and Kin book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T06:53:25-07:00","id":1491294,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491265#post1491265\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Witch's Brambles is a Royal Thorn Contract that lets the user perform Hedgespinning in the mortal realm under certain stipulations. The Witchtooth Trickery allows the changeling to &quot;reshape the land within one mile to look however she wants it to.&quot; What this means pre-errata is a little vague, though does impose a -1 penalty to Survival rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>On the surface and in character these probably look pretty similar, but to me it reads like the Witchtooth blessing is be almost entirely aesthetic (specifically using the word appearance) with an element of confusing people trying to navigate or use familiar materials where hedgespinning with Witch's Brambles is much broader (bonuses, tilts, swarms of bees etc) and can affect real if temporary change. I <i>do </i>feel like the range on the trickery would get weird fast if someone tries to use it in an urban or suburban environment, but if it becomes an issue the ST can always remind players that drawing broad attention to themselves doesn't tend to work out for changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/807-arcadianawakened","name":"ArcadianAwakened","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T07:38:47-07:00","id":1491298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcadianAwakened</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491294#post1491294\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the surface and in character these probably look pretty similar, but to me it reads like the Witchtooth blessing is be almost entirely aesthetic (specifically using the word appearance) with an element of confusing people trying to navigate or use familiar materials where hedgespinning with Witch's Brambles is much broader (bonuses, tilts, swarms of bees etc) and can affect real if temporary change. I <i>do </i>feel like the range on the trickery would get weird fast if someone tries to use it in an urban or suburban environment, but if it becomes an issue the ST can always remind players that drawing broad attention to themselves doesn't tend to work out for changelings.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Witch's Brambles is pretty crazy, as Hedgespinning is already a little nuts but being able to utilize paradigm shifts (which ime, happens a fair amount of the time) in the real world is huge. But honestly, I don't have as much of a problem with Witch's Brambles as do in regards to the Witchtooth blessing. While I understand how the blessing can be seen as &quot;entirely aesthetic,&quot; it does impose a penalty to Survival actions which makes me believe that there is an element of &quot;reality&quot; to it. More concerning is that it covers a square mile, apparently affecting everyone within that range, without a Contest of Wills and no talk of it being an illusion or it being a forgettable thing for normal humans or anything. This is an insane ability for a kith's trickery and at the cost of 1 glamour.<br /> <br /> also, for a point of glamour ... a Draconic can ... fly?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T12:58:49-07:00","id":1491333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491267#post1491267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am designing a chronicle where Edgar Allen Poe is a Darkling with the author kith and his wife, Anna Bell Lee, is a fairest with the Water Kith. Has the Author kith made it into the Kith and Kin book?</div> </div> </div> </div>No and I can give you an exact reason why. Kiths in 2e are meant to be mythic and iconic. An author on its own isn't mythic - its a job. You'll notice that similar Kiths like Dancer, Minstrel, Miner, Brewer, Smith, and Solider aren't in the book either because they are jobs instead of archetypes - although a few of those got a facelift in order to make them more fae. The Brewer has been replaced by the Absinthial, and while their niches are similar, the latter is much more about being a faerie tied to alcohol and intoxication than being a changeling who was forced to learn about brewing - which could honestly just be some dots in Craft and a Specialization. <br /> <br /> (And yes, the Artist did sneak into 2e Core... but that probably wouldn't happen today.) <br /> <br /> So what type of faerie do you want Poe to be? I'd think you'd want the Bricoleur as a faerie who trades in symbolism and creativity, but you could go with something more creative too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:01:39-07:00","id":1491334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Firefly Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491298#post1491298\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">also, for a point of glamour ... a Draconic can ... fly?</div> </div> </div> </div>Draconic gets pretty much three powers, one from the blessing and two from the power. The other power is that either when rending their Mask or in the Hedge they can (possibly; with roll) apply the Terrify condition on those around them.<br /> <br /> There is another kith with essentially three powers, but one of them is hidden in the description. I don't have the book right now so I can't give you their name. Their Mask is essentially their own shadow, rendering them otherwise invisible to anyone and anything that cannot see their mien. I cannot remember what their written power is on top of this.<br /> <br /> I just saw the unintentional humor in that. The power is hidden in the kith description. Heh.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:08:11-07:00","id":1491336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491333#post1491333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Brewer [isn't] in the book either</div> </div> </div> </div>The very first new kith listed in Kith &amp; Kin is essentially a brewer. I wouldn't call it equivalent to Brewer, but it is a job. (Edit: Going to have to agree to disagree on this one; I will become slowly more vocal that the point of the new kiths don\u2019t make a lot of sense to me.) There's another kith that is described as a library guard. Given enough time and wherewithal, I can probably find at least a half dozen new kiths that are jobs. I don't have a problem with this, because a kith can very easily come from the purpose (i.e. job) given to a changeling by their Keeper.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":". 08-25-2022, 04:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:25:04-07:00","id":1491338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491336#post1491336\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The very first new kith listed in Kith &amp; Kin is essentially a brewer. I wouldn't call it equivalent to Brewer, but it is a job. There's another kith that is described as a library guard. Given enough time and wherewithal, I can probably find at least a half dozen new kiths that are jobs. I don't have a problem with this, because a kith can very easily come from the purpose (i.e. job) given to a changeling by their Keeper.</div> </div> </div> </div>Did you read the next sentence where I described the difference between the Brewer and the Absinthial?<br /> <br /> The point isn't that they aren't there, the point is that they are much more than &quot;you did this job in Arcadia.&quot; That was a thing in 1e, but it is not in 2e - the Kith represents what type of fairy the changeling is and how that relates to their self-actualization rather than how their Keeper used them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T13:51:14-07:00","id":1491341,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491338#post1491338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did you read the next sentence where I described the difference between the Brewer and the Absinthial?</div> </div> </div> </div>I added an edit once I noticed this. No need to get snippy. We\u2019re all fans here. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point isn't that they aren't there, the point is that they are much more than &quot;you did this job in Arcadia.&quot; That was a thing in 1e, but it is not in 2e - the Kith represents what type of fairy the changeling is and how that relates to their self-actualization rather than how their Keeper used them. </div> </div> </div>Is it? Because I didn\u2019t get that at all. I spent an evening coming up with a shortened description of each new kith and only a very few of them come off this way to me. I did skip the \u201chow to make a kith\u201d section because as you can tell even here, people want to know more about the new toys. I will go back to that and see if that section unlocks something in my mind, but so far I am, for example, still trying to understand what kind of Durance a Liminal has. From my memory, the exact examples are about what they are made to do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:04:46-07:00","id":1491343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491341#post1491341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is it? Because I didn\u2019t get that at all. I spent an evening coming up with a shortened description of each new kith and only a very few of them come off this way to me. I did skip the \u201chow to make a kith\u201d section because as you can tell even here, people want to know more about the new toys. I will go back to that and see if that section unlocks something in my mind, but so far I am, for example, still trying to understand what kind of Durance a Liminal has. From my memory, the exact examples are about what they are made to do.</div> </div> </div> </div>Given that's what's we were asked to do when writing this book and I talk about it a bit in the section you skipped - yeah it is. If you want to play is the same as 1e, by all means do so, but its not what 2e intends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T14:07:47-07:00","id":1491345,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491343#post1491343\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that's what's we were asked to do when writing this book and I talk about it a bit in the section you skipped - yeah it is. If you want to play is the same as 1e, by all means do so, but its not what 2e intends.</div> </div> </div> </div>And learning what 2e intends is quite high on my list, because it isn\u2019t clear to me from the kith write ups. I sincerely hope this is just a me problem, but I have asked for input from others and without the context of the earlier section I\u2019m getting similar vibes. We shall see!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:00:22-07:00","id":1491350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491333#post1491333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And yes, the Artist did sneak into 2e Core... but that probably wouldn't happen today.)</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know how intentional this was, but for a while I've gotten the feeling that the Artist is meant to serve as a chassis for designing other kiths whose primary theme is hypercompetence in a specific field: Just switch out the Skills mentioned, tweak the name, get ST approval, <i>et puis voil\u00e0</i>, you've got a Chirurgeon or Chauffeur or Choccultist. Ah, the existential horror of being one's job. . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T15:36:22-07:00","id":1491354,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491350#post1491350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't know how intentional this was, but for a while I've gotten the feeling that the Artist is meant to serve as a chassis for designing other kiths whose primary theme is hypercompetence in a specific field: Just switch out the Skills mentioned, tweak the name, get ST approval, <i>et puis voil\u00e0</i>, you've got a Chirurgeon or Chauffeur or Choccultist. Ah, the existential horror of being one's job. . .</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there is something to that. Pallette swapping Artist is certainly a very easy way to build a new Kith","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:16:39-07:00","id":1491364,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491341#post1491341\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I did skip the \u201chow to make a kith\u201d section because as you can tell even here, people want to know more about the new toys. I will go back to that and see if that section unlocks something in my mind, but so far I am, for example, still trying to understand what kind of Durance a Liminal has.</div> </div> </div> </div>The first paragraph-and-a half in that section is pretty direct:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When building a chronicle, kiths provide players and Storytellers the opportunity to make characters unique. <b>Not merely professions that define a changeling\u2019s daily grind,</b> the connective thread of a kith binds a changeling\u2019s history, personality, and theme together. <b>One of the Lost isn\u2019t just a hunter or a doctor;</b> she\u2019s the predator whose eyes gleam between the trees in the dark forest, or an untouchable beekeeper mystic whose bees make honey capable of curing the deadliest illnesses.<br /> <br /> <b>When choosing or creating a kith, remember they always represent the mythic and iconic.</b> Even if the changeling herself remains unaware of this fact, by escaping Arcadia\u2019s clutches, she became nothing short of exceptional, and her struggle to rebuild her life cultivates her individual uniqueness. </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T16:58:18-07:00","id":1491371,"title":"","content":"Hello again Satchel! Good to see you.<br /> <br /> I think I'm starting to see the disconnect. When running and playing 1e, we used kiths as merely the stepping-off point, where the job the Keepers shaped someone for was the foundation upon which the rest of their story was crafted. Poe is a horror writer, so starting with Author was a simple way to go since you could craft the rest of it around that foundation.<br /> <br /> Now the foundation is what kind of story you want to tell with the character. Poe isn't just an author, Poe is a weaver of the macabre, possibly someone who affects what's inside people's minds and makes them see the entire world differently. If they do it with a literary flair, so be it.<br /> <br /> Lovecraft is also an author, but his origins and goal is different. He comes more from a position of the paranoid. He might want to warn people against the horrors of the unknown so they don't want to even leave the house. His kith selection would be quite different.<br /> <br /> To me this makes the list of kiths\u2014appropriately marked Sample Kiths\u2014not as a shopping list but as ideas upon which you can create your own content. If you want to play the kith that's written so be it, but it appears to leave you with more or less origins, Durance, and result played out for you. If this is the intent that explains my reaction to myself; I was hoping more for the core CtL2e book concept of &quot;here is a kith's basic reason for existing; build upon that&quot;.<br /> <br /> Always a pleasure, Satchel.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":".  Better Lovecraft Kith thoughts. 08-25-2022, 07:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:32:29-07:00","id":1491379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491333#post1491333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No and I can give you an exact reason why. Kiths in 2e are meant to be mythic and iconic. An author on its own isn't mythic - its a job. You'll notice that similar Kiths like Dancer, Minstrel, Miner, Brewer, Smith, and Solider aren't in the book either because they are jobs instead of archetypes - although a few of those got a facelift in order to make them more fae. The Brewer has been replaced by the Absinthial, and while their niches are similar, the latter is much more about being a faerie tied to alcohol and intoxication than being a changeling who was forced to learn about brewing - which could honestly just be some dots in Craft and a Specialization.<br /> <br /> (And yes, the Artist did sneak into 2e Core... but that probably wouldn't happen today.)<br /> <br /> So what type of faerie do you want Poe to be? I'd think you'd want the Bricoleur as a faerie who trades in symbolism and creativity, but you could go with something more creative too.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Poe is a Goblin/Sluagh warlock who uses the power of stories to reshape reality. In the chronicle, he fulfills a similar role <span style=\"font-size:12px\">to <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Carapace Clavicle Moundshroud from the <b><i>Halloween Tree.</i></b> He guides for the motley through the Hedge, introduces them to many of the fairy tale characters and spirits connected to Autumn. He even enters Arcadia to confront the True Fae to rescue one of the Motley. At heart, he is a story teller who manipulates events to make an interesting story.<br /> <br /> Since Kiths are mythic and iconic, is there a Banshee kith? Banshee are connected to the foretelling of death and the emotions surrounding death so the Gravewrite kith doesn't quite fit.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T17:48:11-07:00","id":1491381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491379#post1491379\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Poe is a Goblin/Sluagh warlock who uses the power of stories to reshape reality. In the chronicle, he fulfills a similar role <span style=\"font-size:12px\">to <span style=\"color:#202122\"><span style=\"font-family:sans-serif\">Carapace Clavicle Moundshroud from the <b><i>Halloween Tree.</i></b> He guides for the motley through the Hedge, introduces them to many of the fairy tale characters and spirits connected to Autumn. He even enters Arcadia to confront the True Fae to rescue one of the Motley. At heart, he is a story teller who manipulates events to make an interesting story.<br /> <br /> Since Kiths are mythic and iconic, is there a Banshee kith? Banshee are connected to the foretelling of death and the emotions surrounding death so the Gravewrite kith doesn't quite fit.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>It\u2019s not an exact fit, but Poe sounds loosely like a Bricoleur to me \u2014 when writing it I was inspired by stories where fairy tale heroes and heroines transform everyday objects into grand obstacles that resemble their source if you squint (think a number of Baba Yaga tales where someone fleeing her throws a brush or comb down and it turns into a forest). <br /> <br /> There\u2019s no Banshee kith, at least not by the name \u2014 just as 2e has moved away from job kiths, we were asked to move away from culture-themed kiths as well. A lot of kiths are still inspired by specific myths and stories, but you won\u2019t find them under those names.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>chloe \u2022 onyx path freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24091-fiercefully","name":"fiercefully","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T18:46:56-07:00","id":1491386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fiercefully</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491381#post1491381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It\u2019s not an exact fit, but Poe sounds loosely like a Bricoleur to me \u2014 when writing it I was inspired by stories where fairy tale heroes and heroines transform everyday objects into grand obstacles that resemble their source if you squint (think a number of Baba Yaga tales where someone fleeing her throws a brush or comb down and it turns into a forest).<br /> <br /> There\u2019s no Banshee kith, at least not by the name \u2014 just as 2e has moved away from job kiths, we were asked to move away from culture-themed kiths as well. A lot of kiths are still inspired by specific myths and stories, but you won\u2019t find them under those names.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Can you give a description and summary of the Bricoleur kith? not just it's blessing, but also a general summary? I would like to see if it fits with my idea of Poe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-25T18:58:54-07:00","id":1491387,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fiercefully</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491381#post1491381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There\u2019s no Banshee kith, at least not by the name \u2014 just as 2e has moved away from job kiths, we were asked to move away from culture-themed kiths as well. A lot of kiths are still inspired by specific myths and stories, but you won\u2019t find them under those names.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am sorry to hear that. I would have loved to see some of the monsters of Asia and Youkai of Japan reinterpreted as kiths. I am still hoping that we will get a book that focuses on Asia. I would love to see a book that details the courts, freeholds, Hedge, and even True Fae specific to Asia.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T11:07:14-07:00","id":1491431,"title":"","content":"So I was eagerly waiting for this book to finally address the children of changelings. Are they mentioned at all in this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13733-betterworldz","name":"BetterWorldz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13733_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T11:13:48-07:00","id":1491433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BetterWorldz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491431#post1491431\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I was eagerly waiting for this book to finally address the children of changelings. Are they mentioned at all in this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Not in any sense that has particular emphasis, though we do now have systems for Heirlooms, i.e. fae-touched who've inherited their promise from somebody else.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T12:35:13-07:00","id":1491436,"title":"","content":"I am deeply enjoying the first read of the new Regalia. (Up to Scepter.) Kudos!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-26T12:49:02-07:00","id":1491438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491386#post1491386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Can you give a description and summary of the Bricoleur kith? not just it's blessing, but also a general summary? I would like to see if it fits with my idea of Poe.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was hoping someone with a better coherency of these Kith would answer, but let me do my best.<br /> <br /> A Bricoleur seems to be someone who spent their Durance making reality out of symbolism, transforming one thing into another with word-play and other comparisons. The key example in the book is:<div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><i>Bricoleurs are the fairy tale heroes who block their pursuer\u2019s way by throwing combs behind them that become mountains built of teeth or spitting on the ground to create an ocean.</i></div>Their personality is described as non-linear, shunning the literal, and more than a bit competitive about their creativity.<br /> <br /> Their power is to &quot;change a core fact about themselves&quot; that other people &quot;also believe&quot;, though I lament the poor person who is reading my feedback because I am uncertain as to what this means. One of the most interesting side-effects of this is that while it's temporary for the Changeling, whatever core truth they change is permanent for their fetch.<br /> <br /> As far as description, they give Darkling (always looking for things and people to use) and Wizened (carrying around odd collection of things and listening for words to use against people later).<br /> <br /> I hope that helps.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":"change 08-26-2022, 03:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T03:27:47-07:00","id":1491576,"title":"