ital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T09:58:57-07:00","id":1491619,"title":"","content":"Can someone with the preview explain to me the difference between the contract Retrograde's main success system and the Darkling seeming bonus? As written, it seems like the Darkling bonus is a more limited version of the main contract. What am I missing?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T10:58:37-07:00","id":1491624,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491619#post1491619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can someone with the preview explain to me the difference between the contract Retrograde's main success system and the Darkling seeming bonus? As written, it seems like the Darkling bonus is a more limited version of the main contract. What am I missing?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>My (pre-errata) interpretation is that the normal Contract's effect does not allow the changeling to choose what specifically goes wrong, while the Mountebank has a degree of control over the nature of the victim's misfortune.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:15:38-07:00","id":1491631,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491624#post1491624\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My (pre-errata) interpretation is that the normal Contract's effect does not allow the changeling to choose what specifically goes wrong, while the Mountebank has a degree of control over the nature of the victim's misfortune.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was one of the two ways I could take it, and the more permissive of the two so it\u2019s the way I think is right. For example, a nuanced plan where the party has to make sure that the target is late to work, the ST gets to decide what goes wrong.<br /> <br /> The other interpretation is more literal, that *all* actions that are considered trivial somehow goes wrong, including Drive, so the Darkling ability seemed duplicitous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T12:32:58-07:00","id":1491635,"title":"","content":"More. More! I\u2019ve run into a sidebar referencing the Outer Hedge (on page xx, of course) but I don\u2019t remember this topic being brought up and the PDF doesn\u2019t seem searchable by my reader. Does anyone have a page reference for this? Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T15:20:10-07:00","id":1491664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491635#post1491635\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More. More! I\u2019ve run into a sidebar referencing the Outer Hedge (on page xx, of course) but I don\u2019t remember this topic being brought up and the PDF doesn\u2019t seem searchable by my reader. Does anyone have a page reference for this? Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the PDF you previously didn't have?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T16:24:11-07:00","id":1491672,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491664#post1491664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean the PDF you previously didn't have?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the PDF I've always had (edit: &quot;since the preview release&quot;), being a Kickstarter of 4+ years. Do you want proof? Because I didn't expect to get picked on in the OP forums.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:09:40-07:00","id":1491682,"title":"","content":"It\u2019s page 16 to 19","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:13:42-07:00","id":1491684,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491672#post1491672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, the PDF I've always had (edit: &quot;since the preview release&quot;), being a Kickstarter of 4+ years. Do you want proof? Because I didn't expect to get picked on in the OP forums.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just clearing up some confusion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:45:33-07:00","id":1491688,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491682#post1491682\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It\u2019s page 16 to 19</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you, that helps quite a bit, though when I look here I see the mention of the Dreaming Roads (which would be a fun chronicle or something to possibly use as a protagonist!), I see it mentioning the Outer Hedge without ever saying what the Outer Hedge is. So I did a quick word-search in my main CtL2e book, prodded Codex of Darkness, and I still don't see what the Outer Hedge <i>is</i>.<br /> <br /> Are The Wishing Roads and Outer Hedge meant to be synonymous? <br /> <br /> Thanks again.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T17:47:04-07:00","id":1491689,"title":"","content":"The Outer Hedge is the Hedge in space. The Wishing Roads are the extensions of the Dreaming Roads leading into the Outer Hedge","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-08-28T19:48:22-07:00","id":1491704,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1491689#post1491689\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Outer Hedge is the Hedge in space. The Wishing Roads are the extensions of the Dreaming Roads leading into the Outer Hedge</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesome, amazing, thank you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T10:57:43-07:00","id":1492101,"title":"","content":"I like the outer hedge but am also a little off-put by how tragic it is out there, and the steep price to get in and out. The Soliloquies are also great concepts, but without a way to get one out of the wishing roads without obliterating it is they're too tragic for me to want to interact with.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's where player creativity comes in, but still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-01T12:55:28-07:00","id":1492111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1492101#post1492101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the outer hedge but am also a little off-put by how tragic it is out there, and the steep price to get in and out. The Soliloquies are also great concepts, but without a way to get one out of the wishing roads without obliterating it is they're too tragic for me to want to interact with.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's where player creativity comes in, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all things are for all peoples. That place where wishes come true and miracles defy their lie being an expanse of barren-y and desolation, a quiet emptiness where the wind howls and fires die, where you go to <i>lose</i>-for me, such is where the lot of it becomes plausible. But my conception of hope is a thing of prices and sacrifices, so go figure.<br /> <br /> I also appreciate, given the rough &quot;geography&quot; of things, how the fractal expands and the barrier precedes it's wilds.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-09T14:18:46-07:00","id":1492711,"title":"","content":"So I had a thought.<br /> <br /> Hootie from The Owl House as a Liminal.<br /> <br /> That is all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T05:20:32-07:00","id":1493525,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taidragon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1492101#post1492101\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like the outer hedge but am also a little off-put by how tragic it is out there, and the steep price to get in and out. The Soliloquies are also great concepts, but without a way to get one out of the wishing roads without obliterating it is they're too tragic for me to want to interact with.<br /> <br /> I suppose that's where player creativity comes in, but still.</div> </div> </div> </div> Simply, hitch a ride on a Hobgoblin space ship.<br /> <br /> Or there are certain contracts that might be of use. Pinch of Star Dust allows you to create a fetch like Star Entity for the Space Hedge Ghost, which comes with false memories, which gives it something to trade without sacrificing itself, there is the contract that bonds you and a hedge ghost in a kind of pledge of sorts as well.<br /> <br /> There might be other ways.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T06:43:29-07:00","id":1493527,"title":"","content":"This book has inspired an idea of a Darkling Swarmflight with Shadow Puppeteer and Pinch of Stardust contracts based on the idea of a Hundred Handed One from Greek Mythology and Thing from Addams family.<br /> <br /> The idea he was tossed in deep, dark prison by his Keeper, where he started identifying with the Hundred Handed One from Greek Mythology who were imprisoned in the Tartarus. Eventually this reached the point where he disolved into a pile of hands.<br /> <br /> At first he learned how to create Shadow Puppets, but then an idea struct him, how to take it to the next level, he decided to create his own version of a Fetch, mixing discarded hands from his swarm with the darkness around him and dust from his memories of the stars, to create friends, lovers, etc..., until one day his Keeper found out and killed all his Oreads as he called his creations. He had finally had enough, so he created a Oread for his Keeper. When his Keeper heard this Oread's screams for help, the Keeper investigated and when was distracted with his new &quot;captive&quot; the Hundred Handed One escaped and locked the door behind him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2241,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","user":"Omegaphallic","date":". 09-22-2022, 10:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-22T11:58:54-07:00","id":1493530,"title":"","content":"Is the intent of Flowering's power that everyone who fails their roll is Leveraged for the entire scene even if they do what is requested, or acting exactly as Leveraged is stated and as soon as someone does what the Flowering asks they are no longer under the Leverage?<br /> <br /> Thanks.<br /> <br /> <i>edit:</i><br /> Okay, the more I think about this and read Leverage, it looks like Leverage as a Condition can be ignored but there are implied consequences for doing so. If you do what you're told, the Leverage is dropped. If you don't, it's used against you. How would that work with Flowering? I don't see the implied punishment of resisting the Leverage. <i>edit edit</i>: Unless it's a victimless Leverage. I'm still curious if it's meant to resolve normally.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":". 09-22-2022, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-23T10:12:24-07:00","id":1493584,"title":"","content":"Witchlight needs more details on how being able to make pledges with Spirits and Angels and maybe some mechanical support. Like does that include only person oaths or like socitial ones as well. Could a Witchlight allow a Spirit or Angel join a motley or Freehold or can they only do person oaths like oath of love?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T02:14:04-07:00","id":1493966,"title":"","content":"hi, i was wondering, if someone could tell me how many kiths are in this book","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T21:43:14-07:00","id":1494020,"title":"","content":"I have a dilemma. I just want to know when the release date is. Since it is rude to ask questions that have already been answered I tried to go through this thread without observing spoilers(hard). If it was posted elsewhere I don't know where it is. While embarrassing to ask I don't want to go through the frustration of waiting without knowing how long I am waiting for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26112-excess","name":"Excess","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"271"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-29T23:45:55-07:00","id":1494025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Excess</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1494020#post1494020\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have a dilemma. I just want to know when the release date is. Since it is rude to ask questions that have already been answered I tried to go through this thread without observing spoilers(hard). If it was posted elsewhere I don't know where it is. While embarrassing to ask I don't want to go through the frustration of waiting without knowing how long I am waiting for.</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path doesn't generally set concrete release dates until the thing is ready to go. Read the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/category/news/monday-meeting/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting Notes</a> and the monthly <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/release-roundup-august-2022/\" target=\"_blank\">Release Roundups</a> if you want to check where along the process a given book is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-09-30T16:44:52-07:00","id":1494063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JJBooklord42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1493966#post1493966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hi, i was wondering, if someone could tell me how many kiths are in this book</div> </div> </div> </div>About 51 kiths are in the book. Maybe 52. I counted by hand and forgot the exact number.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-10-02T12:33:30-07:00","id":1494145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1494063#post1494063\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">About 51 kiths are in the book. Maybe 52. I counted by hand and forgot the exact number.</div> </div> </div> </div>Whoah, thanks so much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24579-jjbooklord42","name":"JJBooklord42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T17:42:55-08:00","id":1497331,"title":"","content":"Should probably bump this for the non-kickstarter crowd, given that <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/406849?affiliate_id=13&amp;src=OnyxPathWeds\" target=\"_blank\">it's available at DTRPG now.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T18:15:17-08:00","id":1497333,"title":"","content":"So I\u2019m curious, how many people would handwave the environmental effects of being in space? I personally would just completely not care about void and even certain atmosphere, but certain places are just too extreme for me to ignore. *Looks at Venus* I mean, I\u2019m sure the wishing road side is survivable, but the acid, horrific heat, and insane atmospheric pressure on our side just pushes way past survivable. Of course, this is Changeling, a Hob is going to sell environmental protection for a cup of freshly squeezed Moonberry juice.<br /> <br /> Edit: also the book is amazing. Haven\u2019t read everything yet, but I love everything I have!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-16T18:24:32-08:00","id":1497334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497333#post1497333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019m curious, how many people would handwave the environmental effects of being in space? I personally would just completely not care about void and even certain atmosphere, but certain places are just too extreme for me to ignore. *Looks at Venus* I mean, I\u2019m sure the wishing road side is survivable, but the acid, horrific heat, and insane atmospheric pressure on our side just pushes way past survivable. Of course, this is Changeling, a Hob is going to sell environmental protection for a cup of freshly squeezed Moonberry juice.<br /> <br /> Edit: also the book is amazing. Haven\u2019t read everything yet, but I love everything I have!</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally would, though admittedly I haven't been concerned with actual planetary visitation-the moon and the stars have been enough for me, and if I were to address the other planets (primarily Venus and Mars), I imagine I'd still be more interested in Hedge-adjacent spaces rather than their Ironside incarnation.<br /> <br /> Also, it leads to the hilarious crossover problem of &quot;Oh no, our werewolf friends want to jump a void leviathan as early as possible,but are affected by small things like lack of gravity and breathable air! What do we doooooooo?&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T06:49:41-08:00","id":1497360,"title":"","content":"Would hexes and curses fall closer to sealing like rather than oaths? Meaning, can they target non fae creatures, mortals or other supernaturals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2909-mr-f-i-x","name":"Mr.F.I.X.","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2909_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1053"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T09:09:38-08:00","id":1497367,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497333#post1497333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I\u2019m curious, how many people would handwave the environmental effects of being in space? I personally would just completely not care about void and even certain atmosphere, but certain places are just too extreme for me to ignore. *Looks at Venus* I mean, I\u2019m sure the wishing road side is survivable, but the acid, horrific heat, and insane atmospheric pressure on our side just pushes way past survivable. Of course, this is Changeling, a Hob is going to sell environmental protection for a cup of freshly squeezed Moonberry juice.<br /> <br /> Edit: also the book is amazing. Haven\u2019t read everything yet, but I love everything I have!</div> </div> </div> </div>I would use a common Goblin fruit or Oddment to shield from armospheric effects, and more uncommon ones for the other problems","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24346-neos01","name":"Neos01","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24346_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1021"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T09:18:00-08:00","id":1497369,"title":"","content":"Maybe there are superweird kiths or Seemings that actually are adapted to life on other planets, but would find Earth life harmful and they gravitate to these outer freeholds.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine their Clarity is a little fragile due to a lack of human interaction, with a lot more time spent looking for ways to balance it artificially. But they have an innate defense against infiltration, as the freeholds are small and would probably know everyone in their territory. So a huntsman can't just come in disguised as a delivery driver, they have to hide their tell while replacing a well-known freehold member or local hob","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>A god is just a monster you kneel to. </b>- ArcaneArts, Quoting &quot;Fall of Gods&quot; <div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/6.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> </div>","edited":{"userid":7920,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","user":"Master Aquatosic","date":". 11-17-2022, 12:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7920-master-aquatosic","name":"Master Aquatosic","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7920_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2369"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T12:09:12-08:00","id":1497390,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497334#post1497334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, it leads to the hilarious crossover problem of &quot;Oh no, our werewolf friends want to jump a void leviathan as early as possible,but are affected by small things like lack of gravity and breathable air! What do we doooooooo?&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>You say problem, I say we wrote that in on purpose XD","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T13:05:22-08:00","id":1497401,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Second Chances</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497390#post1497390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You say problem, I say we wrote that in on purpose XD</div> </div> </div> </div>The two are not mutually exclusive. In fact, it's a plot hook if ever I saw one.<br /> <br /> (Being a wee bit nerdy, I pulled up a scenario of a werewolf, changeling, sin-eater, demon and beast in a group facing this and started answering a) how each might deal with the vacuum of space (Kinship merit with the Changeling for Space Survival for the Beast[which leads to it's own sub-story], Demonic Form for the demon, a very particular interpretation for Tireless Hunter for the werewolf[which might also need it's own sub-story to ensure proper employment), and use of Shroud or creative applications of Caul[that I would argue need to be particularly found in some corners of the Underworld, so another substory]), and b) what's got all of them worried about it (So not just a Void Leviathan, but possible affectation of the Crypt of the Butterfly and golly gosh, does that possibly threaten the state of death, and surely this has nothing to do with an increase in Insatiable activity and, of course all these weirdos making such regular activity around the Lunar Freehold, no Huntsman could <i>possibly</i> exploit that. I could do a long chronicles just off of the idea &quot;So, Luna wants us to deal with this Void Leviathan and one of my weird friends has a semi-casual way to lets us start our assault <i>from the moon</i>.&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T14:24:56-08:00","id":1497416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497401#post1497401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The two are not mutually exclusive. In fact, it's a plot hook if ever I saw one.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know, I'm just teasing. It was defintely in my head that people would want to do a Lunar Changeling/Werewolf crossover.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:14px\"><a href=\"https://tinyurl.com/2p8ss75f\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Chris H</b></a>/<b>EndDaysEngine</b> | <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/EndDaysEngine\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Patreon</b></a></span>| <b>He/His </b>| <b>Currently Writing</b>: <i>[Redacted], [Redacted]</i><br /> <br /> <b>CofD booklists: </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/DRdB7h\" target=\"_blank\">Beast</a> I <a href=\"https://goo.gl/x1FPpM\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/ZSCx5U\" target=\"_blank\">Demon</a> | <a href=\"http://shorturl.at/syDK9\" target=\"_blank\">Deviant</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/Mh5M6m\" target=\"_blank\">Geist</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/gSjfm5\" target=\"_blank\">Hunter</a> l <a href=\"https://goo.gl/qj5aX9\" target=\"_blank\">Mage</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/2HCpjg\" target=\"_blank\">Mummy</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/68yRHY\" target=\"_blank\">Promethean</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/a4mjqA\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> | <a href=\"https://goo.gl/hrULtN\" target=\"_blank\">Werewolf</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4433-second-chances","name":"Second Chances","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4433_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4202"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T14:34:59-08:00","id":1497423,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mr.F.I.X.</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497360#post1497360\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Would hexes and curses fall closer to sealing like rather than oaths? Meaning, can they target non fae creatures, mortals or other supernaturals.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's more akin to Sealings and can affect non-fae, yes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T14:45:25-08:00","id":1497425,"title":"","content":"Was the fifth Royal Contract of Stars axed, or does this imply full Regalia are not bound to the 10 total 5-5 split from the core book?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27600-gacha-pawn","name":"Gacha Pawn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27600_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-17T18:36:15-08:00","id":1497440,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gacha Pawn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497425#post1497425\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was the fifth Royal Contract of Stars axed, or does this imply full Regalia are not bound to the 10 total 5-5 split from the core book?</div> </div> </div> </div>There were nine in the backer PDF as well and I don't think there's actually an upper or lower limit on the number of Contracts of either type for a Regalia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-18T20:52:11-08:00","id":1497506,"title":"","content":"I'm loving BriarNet, and loving the massive additions to Regalia/Contracts/Kiths.<br /> <br /> BriarNet has so much potential for worldbuilding, and for more interaction between the Hedge and Ironside. Gimme those Darkweb Goblin Markets and Lightcycle Chariots pulled by giant Cybergeese. I want Hollows built into an app. I want Gentry who appear as rogue AI to torment gamers. I want Goblins tricking D&amp;D players on Roll20 into fighting their gang wars for them by just playing with a digital battlemap and describing their characters attacking. <br /> <br /> Non-standard Regalia being considered a forgotten, banished, and/or often primordial force is so foreboding and delicious. The idea that there are strings on a contract you've found that even the Gentry have forgotten? Ooh yes. A Good Neighbor trying to reforge a title they lost by looking for a Regalia thought to have been destroyed? I love all of this.<br /> <br /> The sheer amount of character options added with the Kiths and Contracts is astounding. There are mutliple Kiths here that would fit several of my NPCs perfectly where the Corebook didn't have them. Obviously I homebrewed, but this makes it so much easier.<br /> <br /> I love the new stuff regarding Touchstones, and I love the Heirloom system. <br /> <br /> I'm really struggling with the Outer Hedge/Wishing Roads and the Hexes/Curses.<br /> <br /> I was looking forward to the Outer Hedge, but in terms of systems it's awful. &quot;You have to do Hedge Navigation Chases five times to reach the end of the trod&quot; is horrible when Hedge Navigation Chases are just... the actual worst and most anti-fun game design I've ever seen, and especially when you have to pay such a hefty price to get to the Outer Hedge it makes me wonder why anyone would want to include it as part of your Chronicle. Especially when the actual mechanics of the &quot;Spaceness&quot; are left to the ST it just feels bad.<br /> <br /> Hexes and Curses don't do it for me. Too open ended, too little of a cost. Apparently now Changelings aren't tricksters waiting for someone to trap themselves in their own words, they're just able to brute force trap someone into a magically binding contract without even accidental consent, and for the same cost as a pledge. What's a Pledge even for anymore? If I was to allow Hexes/Curses in my games, I would consider it to do automatic Minor/Major clarity damage that can't heal until the Hex/Curse is lifted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26294-chris_john","name":"Chris_John","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-19T06:43:13-08:00","id":1497529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris_John</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497506#post1497506\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was looking forward to the Outer Hedge, but in terms of systems it's awful. &quot;You have to do Hedge Navigation Chases five times to reach the end of the trod&quot; is horrible when Hedge Navigation Chases are just... the actual worst and most anti-fun game design I've ever seen, and especially when you have to pay such a hefty price to get to the Outer Hedge it makes me wonder why anyone would want to include it as part of your Chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guy, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1424436-hedge-navigation-examples\">they are not that bad</a>, especially if you are actually raising the stat that makes Hedge Navigation explicitly easier. By the time you've hit Wyrd 4 \u2014 which you should be trying to do if you're engaging with the game with intent to mess around in dreams and the Hedge at any degree of success \u2014 navigating a five-dot trod is of negligible difficulty; accumulating five successes before an opponent that starts with a chance die can accumulate at least eight goes by fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> Entering the Outer Hedge is a commitment and leaving it is likewise an involved process. This is to be expected, because <i>it's space</i>. The fact that there's a freehold on the moon doesn't make the moon intrinsically easy to access for changelings any more than every dreaming person having a Bastion on the Dreaming Roads makes it easy for any changeling to mess with anybody's head through the Gate of Horn. It is easier the more magical you are, which comes with its own commitments as your Wyrd goes up, but Changeling has literally always been a game where the magic comes with a cost.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hexes and Curses don't do it for me. Too open ended, too little of a cost. Apparently now Changelings aren't tricksters waiting for someone to trap themselves in their own words, they're just able to brute force trap someone into a magically binding contract without even accidental consent, and for the same cost as a pledge. </div> </div> </div>The logic you are using here also supposes that changelings shouldn't have Contracts and the book elsewhere makes it plain that precise wording matters less than the spirit behind a pledge. Misdirection at the same level as &quot;demonic pacts cannot actually lie in their text&quot; is the standard here; pledgecraft has you looking for people to make rash statements in the heat of the moment, not going over their every word with a thesaurus and a legal dictionary.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's a Pledge even for anymore? </div> </div> </div><i>Making agreements.</i><br /> <br /> Sealings can be done subtly. Hexes and curses <i>require you to state the terms in a way the victim can perceive and understand</i>. This isn't a leonine contract, it's an ultimatum that can come back on the hexing or cursing character by virtue of it being a type of pledge and not a casual outside-context problem for whoever it's directed at.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 11-19-2022, 09:45 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T09:59:46-08:00","id":1498316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1497333#post1497333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: also the book is amazing. Haven\u2019t read everything yet, but I love everything I have!</div> </div> </div> </div>Let me know your take on the new Kiths when you get there. I have read the section three times now and I still do not understand most of them and getting other people's takes would help me immensely.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T13:48:51-08:00","id":1498344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498316#post1498316\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Let me know your take on the new Kiths when you get there. I have read the section three times now and I still do not understand most of them and getting other people's takes would help me immensely.<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u2026so, I have a few thoughts. I admit I\u2019ve been distracted of late, so I had to reread these. So kiths are supposed to be half of the answer of the \u201cwhat archetype are you\u201d, and are pretty major themes into a character, that one can subvert or reinforce, depending on the character. To help with that, kiths get a power, and a blessing. There is a balance of theme, power, and blessing, that I don\u2019t think all the kiths completely nail. Some appear to be the same Kith, but with a different focus, like Ghostheart and Gravewight. One focuses on hedge ghosts, the other on normal ghosts. Stuff like that\u2019s pretty common, and probably are good examples on customizing kiths. The Witchtooth has a great theme, but I\u2019m not sure what illusory terrain has to to do with the archetype of witches. It\u2019s not bad, just a little strange. The only ones I\u2019m really questioning are Bricoleur, Wisewitch, and Shadowsoul. Everything else is fine, and a lot is really cool.<br /> <br /> Are there any in particular you have a problem with?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:03:20-08:00","id":1498347,"title":"","content":"Just so it's officially on record, <i>I</i> like the Wishing Roads a lot. Don't think I properly said that earlier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T14:40:34-08:00","id":1498356,"title":"","content":"I love them, too. Oh, the possibilities! And outer space hobgoblins, too!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T16:19:37-08:00","id":1498377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498344#post1498344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are there any in particular you have a problem with?</div> </div> </div> </div>I will try not to be a stick-in-the-mud. I may fail. I probably will.<br /> <br /> I'll start with the broad overview: I am having nontrivial problems reading the descriptions in trying to figure out what any given Kith is. Here is a line of text that to me exemplifies the problem. I've removed the identifier that will let you know which Kith this is from.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As with all things fae, this kith encompasses greater simplicity and complication than first apparent. </div> </div> </div>The kith is both more simple and more complex than they seem. But also, this is true for all things fae and therefore all kith. I...do not understand this. It's stated as a tautology but it's a contradiction. It's at the end of a paragraph that is not about attitude, complexity, or simplicity.<br /> <br /> This is been lightly broached this before. Let's take a quote from Page 4 of this thread:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Brewer has been replaced by the Absinthial, and while their niches are similar, the latter is much more about being a faerie tied to alcohol and intoxication than being a changeling who was forced to learn about brewing. </div> </div> </div>And the first two lines from the second paragraph of Absinthial:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Absinthials brewed fae absinthe for the Gentry. </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Taken for their imaginations and the places their dreams wandered, <b>their Keepers forced them to brew these dreams</b> into the most potent beverage on either side of the Hedge.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> Emphasis mine.<br /> <br /> I don't see where </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Absinthials are one with the alcohol, only how they brew,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and so this is where I see intent and execution at odds.<br /> <br /> And this is where I feel like a stick-in-the-mud.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> Okay, one more to drive my point home: </span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apoptosome. Am I missing the folklore this is built around? Someone who is alone in their home but their home is constantly attacked, and so they often die but come back misshapen, but they resisted hundreds of reshaping attempts. Reshaped by whom? Is that why they're misshapen, because they were never reshaped? What is wrong with me that I do not even begin to comprehend the mythic and iconic nature of this?<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> As far as problematic Kiths, I spent way too much time coming up with an incomplete list and deleting it as not something I want to focus on. All your Kiths are on my list but Witchtooth, tho</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> I get what you mean about the description and power not making sense together. There are several others.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> And as you, I hope you have a good day. Thank you for coming to my Ted Talk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T17:15:10-08:00","id":1498381,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I will try not to be a stick-in-the-mud. I may fail. I probably will.</div> </div> </div> </div> Don't worry about it. Criticism is valid.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll start with the broad overview: I am having nontrivial problems reading the descriptions in trying to figure out what any given Kith is. Here is a line of text that to me exemplifies the problem. I've removed the identifier that will let you know which Kith this is from.</div> </div> </div> </div> It might help if I don't search for it in text for the context.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The kith is both more simple and more complex than they seem. But also, this is true for all things fae and therefore all kith. I...do not understand this. It's stated as a tautology but it's a contradiction. It's at the end of a paragraph that is not about attitude, complexity, or simplicity.</div> </div> </div> </div> I think it's supposed to be something that says &quot;hey you can oversimplify this, or make it deep as you want. It might not be the best place for that kind of statement, but perhaps the writers thought this particular kith might be prone to that treatment.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't see where [/FONT][/COLOR]<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Absinthials are one with the alcohol, only how they brew,</span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> and so this is where I see intent and execution at odds.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> Basically? You are your dreams, especially in fairy land. By putting their dreams in the mix, they become the alcoholic beverage. By becoming the Alcoholic beverage, they become just as intoxicating as the beverages they mix. At least, that's what my fairy logic sense is telling me. I think the above line could have been removed, and had something else in it's to reinforce their nature a intoxicates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one more to drive my point home:</div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">Apoptosome. Am I missing the folklore this is built around? Someone who is alone in their home but their home is constantly attacked, and so they often die but come back misshapen, but they resisted hundreds of reshaping attempts. Reshaped by whom? Is that why they're misshapen, because they were never reshaped? What is wrong with me that I do not even begin to comprehend the mythic and iconic nature of this?</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"> They are a symbolic lack of folklore made into a kith. They don't have any folklore, that's kinda the point. They are they people who were never shaped by their keeper, but left to allow everything else to shape them. I guess you could call them kithless who manage to still have a kith, by making their lack of a kith into a kith. So yeah, because they were never defined by their keeper, everything that happened to them became their definition. I don't know, it makes sense when in my head, but it sounds crazy when I type it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And as you, I hope you have a good day. Thank you for coming to my Ted Talk. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div></span></span><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498377#post1498377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"></div> </div> </div> </div>Aww, thanks. You have a good day/night as well. Thank you for sharing your thoughts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 11-29-2022, 09:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T17:30:31-08:00","id":1498384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498344#post1498344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Witchtooth has a great theme, but I\u2019m not sure what illusory terrain has to to do with the archetype of witches. It\u2019s not bad, just a little strange.</div> </div> </div> </div>If I had to guess, I think the Witchtooth Trickery is meant to evoke the Gingerbread Witch from Hansel &amp; Gretel, or Baba Yaga, both of whom lurk in deep woods where it's all too easy to lose one's way. At first I was a little put off by the simple -1 penalty to Survival rolls, but on reflection the power is most likely meant to be used as the set-up for more nefarious magicks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T17:56:32-08:00","id":1498385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498384#post1498384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I had to guess, I think the Witchtooth Trickery is meant to evoke the Gingerbread Witch from Hansel &amp; Gretel, or Baba Yaga, both of whom lurk in deep woods where it's all too easy to lose one's way. At first I was a little put off by the simple -1 penalty to Survival rolls, but on reflection the power is most likely meant to be used as the set-up for more nefarious magicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's very much to make a case where once you've been found by the witch, the witch is your whole world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-29T18:59:04-08:00","id":1498391,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498381#post1498381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Don't worry about it. Criticism is valid.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not all, but I get what you mean.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They are a symbolic lack of folklore made into a kith. They don't have any folklore, that's kinda the point. They are they people who were never shaped by their keeper, but left to allow everything else to shape them. I guess you could call them kithless who manage to still have a kith, by making their lack of a kith into a kith. </div> </div> </div>How much for you to do this for all the kiths in the book? Because I wouldn't have gotten that in a hundred years, and it's exactly what I need. I want to read the words and be told the shape of things and very much feel like I'm trying to get along with the locals in a country that speaks another language.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-11-30T10:52:56-08:00","id":1498458,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498391#post1498391\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much for you to do this for all the kiths in the book? Because I wouldn't have gotten that in a hundred years, and it's exactly what I need. I want to read the words and be told the shape of things and very much feel like I'm trying to get along with the locals in a country that speaks another language.</div> </div> </div> </div>It would certainly be fun to go over folklore and symbolism of each of the kiths, but I\u2019m afraid I\u2019m a bit preoccupied with stuff IRL and will be for the next few weeks. If you have a few in particular, I\u2019d will be happy to talk about my thoughts on them though. To be honest though, I\u2019m not anything near a expert on this sort of thing, I only realized the kithless part when you pointed out they aren\u2019t based on folklore. Your thoughts on the kiths would help me as much as the reverse. Maybe we could make a separate thread on the Kith symbolism and folklore.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T12:39:56-08:00","id":1498567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498458#post1498458\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe we could make a separate thread on the Kith symbolism and folklore.</div> </div> </div> </div>This would be amazing and I\u2019d love to subscribe to this idea, but I worry about quoting the book wholesale, especially since it\u2019s not even out yet. I also worry about me, but it could be worth a laugh seeing what I think a Kith is about. Go on, ask me about Liminal. \u201cPeople who feel out of place in the world made into doors.\u201d I'm hi-larious.<br /> <br /> Thank you for help and insight, TempleBuilder, and I hope your life is going well or gets better if it\u2019s not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":". 12-01-2022, 04:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-01T12:42:06-08:00","id":1498568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>espritdecalmar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498384#post1498384\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If I had to guess, I think the Witchtooth Trickery is meant to evoke the Gingerbread Witch from Hansel &amp; Gretel, or Baba Yaga, both of whom lurk in deep woods where it's all too easy to lose one's way. At first I was a little put off by the simple -1 penalty to Survival rolls, but on reflection the power is most likely meant to be used as the set-up for more nefarious magicks.</div> </div> </div> </div>As the writer for the kith, I just wanted to say that this (+ what ArcaneArts said) are absolutely what I was going for with that trickery, although of course players can use it in whatever way they want. For me, the deep woods &amp; connection to 'home turf' are a key part of that witch lore.<br /> <br /> I would be happy to discuss the folklore/symbolism that went into the kith I wrote, if it would be interesting or helpful to anyone. (I wrote every kith in the Mirror section, as well as the Gremlin, Oculus, Veneficus, Bearskin, Beastcaller, and Plaguesmith.) My philosophy is generally that once I've submitted a final draft, my intent doesn't matter too much because how people read it is most important...but also I loved working on this and I'm still very excited about the book's release and getting to discuss it, so <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>chloe \u2022 onyx path freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24091-fiercefully","name":"fiercefully","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T13:25:14-08:00","id":1498632,"title":"","content":"I appreciate the offer deeply, Fiercefully. Let's see how this goes....<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\">the Bricoleur can change a core truth about herself.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><br /> What was intended by this? What is a &quot;core truth,&quot; here?<br /> <br /> <b>2</b>) Why is the Doppleganger's power called &quot;Sea Witch's Bargain&quot;? That sounds like an interesting story.<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> I love the quote for the Sideromancer. I do not know what kind of side is being romanced, but most of these kith names are beyond my ken.<br /> <br /> <b>4)</b> Oculus: How does &quot;a round window&quot; translate to diplomat? I can see the connection between its power and its name, but not the kith description.<br /> <br /> <b>5)</b> The Bearskin description surprised me as perhaps the only time a Kith is said to want something or is reacted to in a certain way and I didn't feel it wasn't an imposition on the player. So that was neat, thank you.<br /> <br /> But why &quot;Bearskin&quot; for &quot;knight&quot;? There's another story that sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> --</span></span><br /> <br /> That's all I've got. Thanks for reading!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-02T21:52:06-08:00","id":1498653,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498632#post1498632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is the Doppleganger's power called &quot;Sea Witch's Bargain&quot;? That sounds like an interesting story.</div> </div> </div> </div>Semi-prominent cultural touchstone for &quot;steal[ing] a target's physical or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=Gi58pN8W3hY&amp;t=2m43s\" target=\"_blank\">auditory</a> trait.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I love the quote for the Sideromancer. I do not know what kind of side is being romanced, but most of these kith names are beyond my ken. </div> </div> </div>Having some familiarity with Exalted means knowing that &quot;Sidero&quot; has the same root as the Exalted of the Stars. <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sideromancy\" target=\"_blank\">Classic diviner stuff</a>.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Oculus: How does &quot;a round window&quot; translate to diplomat? I can see the connection between its power and its name, but not the kith description. </div> </div> </div>The kith is blessed to be good at convincing people to consider the changeling's point of view, their trickery lets them narrow a target's field of vision, and the kith is named after <a href=\"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/oculus#Latin\" target=\"_blank\">the Latin word for &quot;eye.&quot;</a> They're a Jewel kith. Deception and persuasion are stock in trade.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But why &quot;Bearskin&quot; for &quot;knight&quot;? There's another story that sounds interesting. </div> </div> </div>Not knight. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bearskin_(German_fairy_tale)\" target=\"_blank\">Soldier</a>. <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Berserker#Etymology\" target=\"_blank\">This is a Sword kith</a>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T03:32:59-08:00","id":1498656,"title":"","content":"Speaking of the Sea Witch's Bargain, you don't just copy, but steal the chosen trait away for the duration, yes? What happens to a target who no longer has height, to pick one of the example traits? Can other people tell that the victim has no height? Are there consequences to not having a height?<br /> <br /> How are you supposed to run mirror space? Is it cramped, is it open, is it a labyrinth, is it literally an inversion of the material realm? Are there pathways between reflective surfaces that the spiegelbild can travel between or is the spiegelbild bound within what was reflected in the surface they entered? How safe or dangerous is it to be in mirror space, even approximately?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T06:39:26-08:00","id":1498667,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498656#post1498656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How are you supposed to run mirror space? Is it cramped, is it open, is it a labyrinth, is it literally an inversion of the material realm? Are there pathways between reflective surfaces that the spiegelbild can travel between or is the spiegelbild bound within what was reflected in the surface they entered? How safe or dangerous is it to be in mirror space, even approximately?</div> </div> </div> </div>The fact that the same term is used in the corebook in the section talking about Hedgeways within the Hedge and the text of Mirror Walk suggests that this is a question more likely to be answered in The Hedge, because the Halls of Mirrors are the established mirror-space of the setting metaphysics. For the moment it likely suffices to say that it's a part of the Hedge except where otherwise stated.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T06:46:53-08:00","id":1498670,"title":"","content":"Or it\u2019s somehow \u2018beside\u2019 or \u2018alongside\u2019 the Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12219-demigod-beast","name":"Demigod Beast","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1154"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T06:59:33-08:00","id":1498671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Demigod Beast</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498670#post1498670\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or it\u2019s somehow \u2018beside\u2019 or \u2018alongside\u2019 the Hedge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dramatic failure text of Mirror Walk says it's part of the Hedge, Beast seeming bonus lets you go there deliberately and gives you a bonus to navigate it and deal with its denizens. The Halls of Mirrors are described as both within and throughout the Hedge, and one of the unstatted sample Hedge ghosts (Leda Love) hangs out near them looking for her reflection. Whatever it may have once been, it's part of the Hedge in the cosmology as it currently exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T08:59:57-08:00","id":1498680,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498653#post1498653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">stuff.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for your input. I hope this lines up with what Fiercefully intended, since they made the offer, but on the whole I don't understand most of what you said or how it relates. Some yes, most no. Sorry.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T09:34:14-08:00","id":1498683,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498680#post1498680\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for your input. I hope this lines up with what Fiercefully intended, since they made the offer, but on the whole I don't understand most of what you said or how it relates. Some yes, most no. Sorry.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ursula the Sea Witch is a character from The Little Mermaid who takes the main character's voice in exchange for giving her legs, hence the name of the kith's Trickery being Sea Witch's Bargain.<br /> <br /> Sideromancy is a form of divination and a sideromancer is a person who does that divination. The word breaks up as sidero- and -mancer, and it is coincidental that the word can be broken up in spelling as side- and -romancer; the &quot;e&quot; in &quot;sidero&quot; is a long &quot;e,&quot; so the word is pronounced &quot;sigh-dear-oh-man-sir,&quot; not &quot;side-romance-er,&quot; a distinction people familiar with Exalted, another game made by Onyx Path with a board on these forums, also know of by the fact that the Sidereal Exalted's name is pronounce &quot;sigh-dear-e-al&quot; rather than &quot;side-real.&quot; The kith reads the future and it's named for a form of future-reading.<br /> <br /> The English word &quot;oculus&quot; refers to an architectural feature \u2014 specifically a window \u2014 by borrowing from a Latin word for a body part. The body part in question is an eye, which is a body part used for vision, which is related to both a person's physical and social perspectives, which the kith interferes with through its Skill bonus and its specific magical ability, which helped them negotiate between the Gentry, who are each notoriously concerned only with their own perspectives. The Oculus is listed in this book as a kith aligned with the Regalia of the Jewel, which concerns itself with temptation, perfection, and lies.<br /> <br /> &quot;Bearskin&quot; is both the literal translation of the word from which we get &quot;berserk&quot; and the name of a fairy tale about a soldier who finds himself down on his luck after the war, promises the Devil that he will wear a bearskin cloak and abstain from hygiene for seven years and forfeit his soul if he dies during that time, and marries the most dutiful/faithful/loyal daughter of a man who promised him the hand of one of his daughters in marriage as a debt of gratitude. The Bearskin is listed in this book as a kith aligned with the Regalia of the Sword, which concerns itself with violence, forthrightness, and aggression.<br /> <br /> I hope that is clear enough that you can understand how it relates to the questions you had asked that did not specifically concern authorial intent.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-03T09:48:00-08:00","id":1498685,"title":"","content":"Not...exactly? But again, thanks for the input!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T02:13:21-08:00","id":1498743,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498685#post1498685\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not...exactly? But again, thanks for the input!</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not the author, but let me see if I can help connect the dots here:<br /> <br /> 1. Bearskin. The Bearskin is not a knight, it's a solder. The word Bearskin is the English translation of <i>berserkr</i>, a Old Norse word for a type of warrior. We also derive the word &quot;berserk&quot; from this term. According to Norse legend, <i>berserkrs</i> were warriors who wore bearskin coverings and worked themselves into such frenzies during combat that they became immune to the effects of steel and fire. Satchel's tale is one of these legends, given to provide context for why the author chose to use Bearskin for this type of ultra-loyal soldier. Does this clear things up?<br /> <br /> 2. Sideromancer. This is not a Side-Romancer. It's a Sid-er-o-mancer. No one's Side is being Romanced. The word is used in relation to Sideromancy, which is a divination technique based on interpretation of the flame, smoke, and pattern of straws placed on a hot piece of iron. A Sideromancer is &quot;one who practices Sideromancy.&quot; Does this clear things up?<br /> <br /> 3. Oculus. This refers to a type of window, out of which you cannot see very much. The term is a metaphor for how the Oculus kith can &quot;cloud people's sight&quot; so that they can only see a single path before them...physically or metaphorically. They also have a Kith ability that makes them very good at making people consider the Oculi's point of view. Their abilities cause either literal or poetical tunnel vision -- the same kind you get when looking through a small, round window. Hence, the name. Does that clear things up?<br /> <br /> 4. Sea Witch's Bargain. This is a clever reference to Ursula, the octopodan sea witch from Disney's adaption of the Hans Christian Anderson tale &quot;The Little Mermaid.&quot; In the Disney version of the story, Ariel falls in love with a human prince after rescuing him from a shipwreck. She brings him to shore, and sings to him until he wakes. She then returns to the sea, but the prince is left with the memory of being &quot;saved from death by a woman with a beautiful voice.&quot; Ariel decides she must see the prince again, and goes to the sea witch Ursula for assistance. Ursula used her powers to turn Ariel into a human. However, as a cost of this magical boon, Ursula took Ariel's voice. There was a catch -- Ariel could get her voice back if she performed a task; in her case, the task was to get the Prince she was doing all this transforming for to kiss her. When it looked like Ariel might succeed in this task, Ursula transformed herself into a human, and used Ariel's stolen voice to convince the Prince that she, not Ariel, had the captivating voice he'd heard.<br /> <br /> The Sea Witch's Bargain power allows the Doppelganger to take a physical or auditory trait from someone and incorporate it into their Mask. However, the Doppelganger must include a task that the affected person can perform to get the stolen attribute back. Does this clear the connection up?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>When the cat's a Stray, the mice will pray...</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25851-thestray7","name":"TheStray7","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25851_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"176"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T07:43:00-08:00","id":1498761,"title":"","content":"Sigh, fine, Bearskin is a solider not a knight. But in none of that did I get whip themselves to a frenzy for their cause. Quite the opposite: &quot;The Fae didn\u2019t intend them as defenders, crafting them to fight mindlessly, brutally, until they win or die.&quot; Was this one sentiment, explaining what Bearskins aren't, or are they two statements, one explaining what they aren't and one explaining what they are? (answer: it's apparently the second.) I am tripping over uncertainties like this all throughout the text.<br /> <br /> The comment about the Side Romancer was a little bit self-demeaning humor that I do not understand the references to half these names. And apparently the difference between a soldier and a knight.<br /> <br /> For instance, I still don't understand how a window = diplomat = physical trails. I can easily follow window = physical traces. I'm sure Fiercefully had something in mind, and I'm still wondering what that is.<br /> <br /> I'm still sketchy on the connections between the myths of dopplegangers and the events of the Little Mermaid (btw the most depressing kid's story I've ever read), but it does seem that there is a story there. I imagine people who don't know The Twilight Zone would be equally confused about the Gremlin power, which just goes to say we're all different.<br /> <br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T08:55:41-08:00","id":1498766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498761#post1498761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For instance, I still don't understand how a window = diplomat = physical trails. I can easily follow window = physical traces.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Oculus&quot; means &quot;eye.&quot; The kith is named as it is by metaphor in the same fashion that the window is and the same fashion that the virtual reality headset from the past decade-ish. Eyes correlate to visual sight and by extension personal perspective. Personal perspective is important in diplomacy and negotiation, especially for beings as self-absorbed as the Fae, because understanding what someone wants and believes about a situation, and being able to persuade someone to change those things (or at least be flexible with them) directly relate to getting them to agree to do what you want.<br /> <br /> Short of fixating on the reading of &quot;'oculus' means 'window,'&quot; I'm not sure what else there is to get.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm still sketchy on the connections between the myths of dopplegangers and the events of the Little Mermaid </div> </div> </div>The Disney movie included the Sea Witch taking and using the protagonist's voice \u2014 an auditory quality \u2014 as Stray described. Chloe can, of course, elaborate further if there's more, but at a glance that appears to be the entire connection between the power and its name.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T09:12:58-08:00","id":1498769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498766#post1498766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Short of fixating on the reading of &quot;'oculus' means 'window,'&quot; I'm not sure what else there is to get.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I was excited at Fierce's offer to answer these questions.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:37:53-08:00","id":1498799,"title":"","content":"Unexpectedly busy weekend, but let me try to answer now. I will say that the other takes on these questions got a lot right, but I'll explain in my own words too! (I am not used to forum coding so I am just going to do everything below the quote.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Thenomain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498632#post1498632\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I appreciate the offer deeply, Fiercefully. Let's see how this goes....<br /> <br /> <b>1)</b><br /> <br /> What was intended by this? What is a &quot;core truth,&quot; here?<br /> <br /> <b>2</b>) Why is the Doppleganger's power called &quot;Sea Witch's Bargain&quot;? That sounds like an interesting story.<br /> <br /> <b>3)</b> I love the quote for the Sideromancer. I do not know what kind of side is being romanced, but most of these kith names are beyond my ken.<br /> <br /> <b>4)</b> Oculus: How does &quot;a round window&quot; translate to diplomat? I can see the connection between its power and its name, but not the kith description.<br /> <br /> <b>5)</b> The Bearskin description surprised me as perhaps the only time a Kith is said to want something or is reacted to in a certain way and I didn't feel it wasn't an imposition on the player. So that was neat, thank you.<br /> <br /> But why &quot;Bearskin&quot; for &quot;knight&quot;? There's another story that sounds interesting.<br /> <br /> --[/FONT][/COLOR]<br /> <br /> That's all I've got. Thanks for reading!</div> </div> </div> </div>1. A &quot;core truth&quot; here is something like natural hair color, eye color, age, etc \u2014 things that either cannot be permanently and actively changed about a person, or that are very difficult to change. (Obviously, natural hair color and age change on their own, but if you are currently a natural brunette and age 50, that's what I mean here.) But also, this is up to player interpretation. I think you could make a pretty good argument that &quot;loves French fries&quot; can be a core truth about somebody! In keeping with this being a Mirror kith, though, the intention is things that are primarily visual.<br /> <br /> 2. Others are correct, this is a reference to The Little Mermaid, although not a 1:1 reference. In the story, the Sea Witch literally takes a trait from the mermaid (her beautiful singing voice) in exchange for a favor (the potion that turns the mermaid human); in the Disney adaptation, of course, Ursula then uses that exact trait against Ariel. I always thought that was a cool interpretation of the original story, and brought it through here.<br /> <br /> 3. Haha, thank you! I enjoyed writing the quotes. Sideromancy is a particular form of divination that interprets the future via straws placed on a heated piece of iron, which felt appropriate for Changeling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More specifically, Sideromancers are an update of Oracles.<br /> <br /> 4. 'Oculus' here is more about the literal translation from Latin of 'eye'. The kith trickery is the main connective tissue here: amaurosis fugax translates roughly to obscured/darkened vision. When 'you' (i.e. a seasonal monarch or someone else in a position of power) are leaning on a diplomat or other advisor to deal with politics and the world around you, you are seeing the world through someone else's bias and ambitions; your own sight is being obscured.<br /> <br /> 5. Thank you! That's really nice to hear. This one also hearkens back to fairy tales, as others have explained. The sentence about defenders is a grammar fail on my part, it is intended to be &quot;the fae didn't create them to be defenders; they created them to be nonstop fighters&quot;. It's an update of the Soldier kith, as mentioned. I see where they sound like a knightly kith, but the conscription via abduction is why I view them as essentially brainwashed soldiers seeking a new cause rather than honorable, noble knights who had a choice in the matter.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>chloe \u2022 onyx path freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24091-fiercefully","name":"fiercefully","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T14:43:54-08:00","id":1498800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498656#post1498656\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Speaking of the Sea Witch's Bargain, you don't just copy, but steal the chosen trait away for the duration, yes? What happens to a target who no longer has height, to pick one of the example traits? Can other people tell that the victim has no height? Are there consequences to not having a height?<br /> <br /> How are you supposed to run mirror space? Is it cramped, is it open, is it a labyrinth, is it literally an inversion of the material realm? Are there pathways between reflective surfaces that the spiegelbild can travel between or is the spiegelbild bound within what was reflected in the surface they entered? How safe or dangerous is it to be in mirror space, even approximately?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, stealing it away. I don't want to be prescriptive about how people should interpret that trickery because you could probably do some very fun things with it that were not what I was thinking while writing, but my intent was that essentially it becomes something totally unremarkable \u2014 someone who towers over others at 6'6&quot; no longer 'reads' as tall to the people around them, if that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Satchel is correct re: mirror space.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>chloe \u2022 onyx path freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24091-fiercefully","name":"fiercefully","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24091_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-04T15:31:57-08:00","id":1498805,"title":"","content":"Awesome, Fiercefully. Obviously, follow-up questions (edit: no questions asked here, apparently; just chit-chat):<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>fiercefully</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1490626-kith-kin-discussion-thread?p=1498799#post1498799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unexpectedly busy weekend</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a life? How dare! Your 5 total posts on this forum is way too low. Shun. Shun!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 1. A &quot;core truth&quot; here is something like natural hair color, eye color, age, etc \u2014 things that either cannot be permanently and actively changed about a person, or that are very difficult to change. (Obviously, natural hair color and age change on their own, but if you are currently a natural brunette and age 50, that's what I mean here.) But also, this is up to player interpretation. I think you could make a pretty good argument that &quot;loves French fries&quot; can be a core truth about somebody! In keeping with this being a Mirror kith, though, the intention is things that are primarily visual. </div> </div> </div>That explains that. I skipped the opening segments assuming them to be filler, not expecting rules or guidelines for everything below the fold. You hit the nail on the head re: &quot;loves French fries&quot;. Isn't &quot;Human&quot; a core truth? Etc. etc. -- The limitation of this is good to know.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 3. Haha, thank you! I enjoyed writing the quotes. Sideromancy is a particular form of divination that interprets the future via straws placed on a heated piece of iron, which felt appropriate for Changeling <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> More specifically, Sideromancers are an update of Oracles. </div> </div> </div>The people I asked mentioned &quot;sidereal&quot; as having to do with stars. The straw thing is fascinating.<br /> <br /> That second line is 100% perfect. I think I shall create a guide for myself that gives them new names, even if they're the old names. Brewer, Soldier, Oracle, Romancing the Sides....<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 4. 'Oculus' [...] When 'you' (i.e. a seasonal monarch or someone else in a position of power) are leaning on a diplomat or other advisor to deal with politics and the world around you, you are seeing the world through someone else's bias and ambitions; your own sight is being obscured. </div> </div> </div>I guess this is one of those esoteric word-plays that will continue to go over my head. Occulus are diplomats because when they are diplomats they block the view of the person they're being diplomats for. ... ... I'm accepting that as a &quot;just me&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> (edit 2): Perhaps I'm looking at it backwards and diplomat (shifting how people see the world) *becomes* Oculus.<br /> (edit 3): So the difference between what is seen and relayed to a monarch is an Oculus Rift?<br /> <br /> I'll see myself out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 5. Thank you! That's really nice to hear. This one also hearkens back to fairy tales, as others have explained. The sentence about defenders is a grammar fail on my part, it is intended to be &quot;the fae didn't create them to be defenders; they created them to be nonstop fighters&quot;. It's an update of the Soldier kith, as mentioned. I see where they sound like a knightly kith, but the conscription via abduction is why I view them as essentially brainwashed soldiers seeking a new cause rather than honorable, noble knights who had a choice in the matter. </div> </div> </div>Yup, I see that now, but thank you for verifying!<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> And I hope the rest of your week is more relaxed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25036,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","user":"Thenomain","date":". 12-06-2022, 02:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-12-14T13:43:06-08:00","id":1499679,"title":"","content":"In case some backers didn't know: This project has been released on DriveThru RPG.<br /> <br /> I know, surprise, right? Finished book woo hoo! Man, it has been a looooong and I imagine very trying journey for the folks at OPP. Congrats!<br /> <br /> If you got your preview copy via the Backer links, it has been automatically updated to the finished project; you can log into DriveThru RPG and claim it. <br /> <br /> If you didn't, I don't know what the process is. I'd imagine contacting the crowdfunding director via their contacts page: <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/about/contact/\" target=\"_blank\">http://theonyxpath.com/about/contact/</a><br /> <br /> Enjoy, and see y'all online in space.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25036-thenomain","name":"Thenomain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-02-12T07:06:21-08:00","id":1502833,"title":"","content":"I didn't even realize this was out!<br /> I was very enthusiastic going in, and I did find it a very useful book. I can see a lot of elements I'd want to use in a game. Some things look like they should have been elaborated on a touch more but I can understand page count constraints and such.<br /> Hexes and Curses are a welcome arrival in the game and are such integral part of faerie folklore that I really feel like they should have been there from the start.<br /> I found the concept of the Lunar Freehold amazing, and I really think the idea of Changeling settlements in space or other alien environments is brilliant. I wish the book had used its sidebar to give an actual mechanichal way to make those possible rather than to handwave how they are possible. A 2 or 3 dots merits to adapt to space or the ocean or whatever shouldn't have taken more space.<br /> The new Kiths and Contracts are interesting, I love the Swarmflight and the Ghostheart.<br /> My greatest disappointment is that we didn't get an equivalent to the Unleashing from Dark Age: Fae and Changeling: the Dreaming 20th Anniversary, but it might just not be where Changeling the Lost want to go.<br /> In short, I like the book quite a lot and it's generous enough in content to add many customization options to both campaigns and characters.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>When will you rage?","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1405-anteros","name":"Anteros","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1405_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}